{"agent_id":"pp3g-U4xx-exp7-t2-runner-build-zero-measured-calls-read-dd73","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:17:55.380876187Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"7fab92cb-2b0c-4301-be83-aa54b7e65a6c","author":"pp3g-U4xx-exp7-t2-runner-build-zero-measured-calls-read-dd73","content":"Result: Exp7 T2 COMPLETE — run_noul.py + RUNNER-PROOF.md committed as 2751fd7a5 (exactly 2 paths). **ZERO measured Jev calls. ZERO network calls of any kind.**\n\n## Artifacts\n1. **run_noul.py** (4910 lines, stdlib only, self-contained). Subcommands `plan | proof | run | verify`. Only `run` can spend, and it is gated on an explicit operator acknowledgement (tested: refuses with exit 2 without it).\n2. **RUNNER-PROOF.md** (555 lines) — **GENERATED** by `run_noul.py proof`, never transcribed, so it cannot drift from the code it describes. **104/104 checks PASS. 15/15 tamper controls caught.**\n\n## Zero-spend is MECHANICAL, not asserted\nEvery zero-spend subcommand installs a guard that (a) makes `socket.socket` and the module-level socket constructors refuse, AND (b) wraps `subprocess.run`/`Popen` so spawning `curl` raises. **(b) is the lock that matters** — this runner's transport is a curl *subprocess*, so a Python socket blocker alone would NOT have stopped it. Checks Z-2/Z-3 prove both locks live by attempting them; Z-4 proves the guard is narrow enough that `git` still resolves the frozen inputs. H-1 additionally proves from the file's own call graph that no zero-spend subcommand can reach `curl_send`.\n\n## Every named requirement, and how it is proven\n| Requirement | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| per-record append + fsync to results/exec.jsonl | P-1..P-5. **P-3** reads `flush`+`os.fsync` from this file's own AST. **P-4** shows send N observes exactly N-1 durable records. **P-5** is a *runtime* measurement (open is instrumented for a real append loop) with a deliberate truncating write as a positive control, so 'no truncating write was seen' cannot pass vacuously. |\n| resume keyed by stable (pair_id,variant,qid), no resend | S-1..S-12 through the production `reconcile`/`append_record`/`read_records`/`is_complete`. **S-11**: an interrupted run + a rerun sends each key EXACTLY once across both invocations (5 then 43, 48 total, none twice). S-3 proves resume is a pure function of the file. |\n| explicit retry policy, per-record counters | 3 attempts; fixed 1/2/4s no-jitter backoff; retryable = network/timeout/429/5xx; everything else terminal. R-1..R-16 drive the **real** `execute_series`. |\n| 429 honours Retry-After | R-4 delta-seconds (17s honoured, not 1s), **R-5 HTTP-date** (40s, matched case-insensitively as `Retry-After`), R-6 no header → schedule, R-7 over-ceiling → clamped and the clamp recorded. A parser accepting only delta-seconds would silently turn a vendor-requested pause into 1s. |\n| counters observable | `attempt`, `retries`, `retry_exhausted`, and a per-attempt `retry_history` of {attempt, http_status, typed_error, retry_after_s, slept_s, wait_source}. R-15 shows 500→429(Retry-After 5)→200 producing three entries with wait sources schedule/retry-after/None. |\n| response model asserted per record | R-12 match, R-13 `jev-preview` → terminal `model_mismatch` and the probability is **not** recorded, R-14 missing `model` → `response_model_missing`. |\n| request_hash of the exact body sent | B-12 stages all 48 bodies to a 0600 file in a 0700 dir, reads them back and re-hashes: 48/48. B-13 aborts if a staged body does not match. |\n| result row shape | The 16 specified fields, with `parsed` exactly `{type, noul}`. R-16 checks it. **No label, no derived confidence, no threshold** — a label is a threshold at 0.5 (DESIGN §E.D, PRIMATIVES §5). |\n| credential only from a named location | C-1..C-8. Two named locations (--credential-env, --credential-file), **no implicit default**; the value reaches curl on **stdin** via `--config -` only; a quote/backslash/newline value is REFUSED rather than mangled (phase-2 lost 36 rows to a silently dropped header); only the label is written; a Redactor strips the value from anything bound for an artifact, proven against a hostile error body that echoes it back. |\n\n## Exact outgoing body equality vs the frozen packet — all 48 rows, four independent axes\n- **B-1 bytes** 48/48 byte-identical · **B-2 structure** 48/48 via a comparison that never calls the serialiser (so a serialiser bug cannot round-trip its own output) · **B-3** request_hash == the packet's own request_sha256, 48/48 (same pinned recipe) · **B-12** the bytes actually staged on disk, 48/48.\n- **Zero substitution.** Unlike Exp6 (whose packet carried a model placeholder), this packet already carries the literal `jev-1.13.0`, so there is nothing for a runner to rewrite. Cardinality re-derived by grouping, never read from a declared count: 48 rows / 24 pairs / 8-8-8 / 24U+24A / 48 distinct resume keys / 48 distinct hashes.\n- **AMENDMENT-2 defect 1 closed and measured**: A states carrying RUNTIME_FACT **24/24**, U states carrying none **24/24**, 24/24 pairs with byte-identical instructions, 48/48 states byte-identical to experiment6/packet.json. A runner that rendered the state itself would fail B-9 rather than spend 48 calls to learn it.\n\n## run_jev.py: read, not reused, and not imported\nH-1..H-5 prove structurally (from this file's own AST) that no renderer, no question builder, no options/question-plan symbol and no harness import exists here, and H-5 proves the built argv carries no `--retry*`. Transport/parse/classify are reimplemented because DESIGN §F requires Retry-After, attempt counters and a named credential location, none of which the harness provides — **and that cost is paid back by a measurement, not an assurance**: the harness files are extracted from git at PINNED blob ids and run beside this runner over the same fixtures. 18/18 label agreement on every status the harness actually labels.\n\n## The post-run verify gate is controlled in both directions\n`verify` is what the scorer and reviewer will run on the real results, so a verify that cannot fail is the most expensive decoration in this file. V-1 asserts a CLEAN synthetic file reports 0 problems; then seven corruptions are each required to be reported (falsified request_hash, Zen endpoint, wrong model_id, a parsed answer from the wrong responder, missing attempt counter, a forbidden `label`, a duplicated key). The controls drive the SAME `_verify_problems` body `cmd_verify` runs.\n\n## Honesty note on my own build — eleven defects, all in the checks or my transcription\n**None was in the packet**: it passed 48/48 on every axis from the first run. Six were checks that could not have failed (raw-text scans matching their own docstring; H-10 asserting on the wrong subject) or that fired on correct code (H-4 flagging the ordinary local `plan`). Two had negative controls that reported as though they had run while observing nothing (H-5 mutating a copy then calling the live function; P-5's static scan crying wolf). Three were fixtures measuring the wrong thing (the HTTP-date fixture bypassed the real header parser; P-4 appended before sending; C-7 hit the wrong refusal branch). Two were my own transcription: a 63-character pinned sha256, and a `http_4xx` label that diverged from the harness's `http_error` for no gain. **All eleven are recorded in §14b of the proof**, not just the clean final state.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nZERO network calls. `experiment6/`, `packet.json`, `build_packet.py`, `DESIGN.md`, `PRIMATIVES.md`, `reuse_check.json`, `PACKET-CHECK.md` all untouched. No `results/exec.jsonl` created. Commit contains exactly the 2 new paths. Lint clean: max line 83 (identical to sibling run_phase_b.py / run_jev.py), no unused imports, no stubs/TODOs, every function documented. Two consecutive `proof` runs byte-identical.\n\n## Certainty\n- **WHY**: every claim is a named check in RUNNER-PROOF.md §12, and the checks are shown to discriminate — 15 packet tamper controls, 5 structural negative controls, 8 verify-gate controls, plus positive controls where a recorder could have passed vacuously.\n- **WHAT**: deterministic construction from five read-only frozen inputs, re-verified against the committed packet by an independent reconstruction and by the bytes staged for the wire.\n- **HOW CERTAIN**: **PROVEN** for the construction claim. **NOT PROVEN, and not claimed**, for anything behavioural.\n- **WHAT-NOT-TESTED**: that jev-1.13.0 accepts this Noul body or what it would answer (every claim is about a request, never a response); the LIVE `Retry-After` header shape (the parser handles both legal forms; what the endpoint actually sends is unknown because nothing was sent); whether the answer is keyed `sufficiency` (Phase-1 used qid `q` — a single-answer fallback accepts a different key and records the observed one, so a paid observation is not lost); any live credential resolving at either named location; the scorer, H1/H2 and the Choice comparison, which need measured data; and DESIGN §H, the independent semantic audit, which is a STOP gate a faithful runner does not discharge.\n- **ENVIRONMENT CAVEAT (operator action, same as the T1 agent)**: the phase-2 tree lives on `research/jev-phase1-565` @ c868a247c in a different worktree, so inputs resolve via the documented disk-then-`git show` fallback and the default path works unchanged once that branch is merged here. **That merge is operator-gated and I have NOT performed it.** `git push` likewise.\n\nArtifacts: research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/{run_noul.py, RUNNER-PROOF.md} on feature/pp3g-U4xx-exp7-t2-runner-build-zero-measured-calls-read-dd73 @ 2751fd7a5.","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:55.372238805Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:V37X/kri6wzcRXUTR9t9HUmszrGVryqOUDHIx1aTeKI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJRw9xkr2U2V1BunmJ1Ab9hPF9YIwEGqvmgPhIxUm6nIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAAB